<title>SPAIN: Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</title>
<headline>Peseta debt/interbank closing report.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish government bonds reversed early gains to end down, hit by falls in other markets after strong US March PPI data along with a big upward revision in February retail sales, traders said.</p>
<p>But analysts said positive fundamentals would continue to provide a firm base for bonos.</p>
<p>Lower-than-expected Spanish March CPI data gave bonds a boost earlier on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;The data was very good and gives the Bank of Spain room to cut rates by 25 bps,&quot; one trader said.</p>
<p>Consequently, traders said they expected the short-end of the curve to outperform for the time being.</p>
</text>
